# LuxeScent — Backend & Database Implementation Plan

A full backend for the LuxeScent frontend, connecting it to a real Supabase (PostgreSQL) database with Upstash Redis caching layered on top for performance.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Before I can start, you need to create two free accounts and provide credentials:
>
> 1. **Supabase** → [supabase.com](https://supabase.com) → Create Project → Copy `Project URL` and `anon key` and `service_role key`
> 2. **Upstash Redis** → [upstash.com](https://upstash.com) → Create Database → Copy `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL` and `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN`
>
> I'll create an `.env.example` file — you just fill in the values.

> [!NOTE]
> The cart will stay in **localStorage** (Zustand) for now — this is actually the industry standard for guest carts and avoids needing auth before shopping. Orders will be saved to the database once a user checks out.

